;; Mexican chart of accounts — SAT Código Agrupador starter set.
;;
;; The Servicio de Administración Tributaria (SAT) publishes a
;; mandatory taxonomy (the "Código Agrupador del SAT") that every
;; Mexican filing entity must map their internal chart to for the
;; Contabilidad Electrónica monthly filing (catálogo de cuentas XML
;; per Anexo 24 of the Resolución Miscelánea Fiscal). The taxonomy
;; uses a 3-digit account group + 3-digit subaccount + (optional)
;; 3-digit sub-subaccount, dot-separated.
;;
;; Top groups (Código Agrupador SAT):
;;   100  Activos circulantes              (current assets)
;;   110  Activos fijos                    (fixed assets)
;;   119  Impuestos acreditables (IVA ITC) — split cobrado / no cobrado
;;   200  Pasivos a corto plazo            (short-term liabilities)
;;   208  Impuestos trasladados (output IVA / IEPS) — split cobrado / no cobrado
;;   300  Pasivos a largo plazo            (long-term liabilities)
;;   400  Capital contable                 (equity)
;;   401  Capital social + Utilidades Retenidas
;;   500  Ingresos                         (revenue)
;;   600  Costos                           (cost of sales)
;;   700  Gastos                           (operating expenses)
;;   800  Otros ingresos / gastos
;;   900  Cuentas de orden                 (memo accounts)
;;
;; Cash-basis IVA — the critical MX specific.
;;
;; Mexico recognises IVA on a CASH basis (Art. 1-B Ley del IVA). The
;; supplier owes output IVA to SAT only when payment is received from
;; the customer; until then it sits in a holding account ("no
;; cobrado"). Symmetrically, the buyer claims input IVA credit only
;; when payment goes out ("pagado"). The chart reflects this by
;; splitting each side:
;;
;;   208.01.xxx  IVA trasladado COBRADO        — output IVA, owed to SAT
;;   208.02.xxx  IVA trasladado NO COBRADO     — output IVA, pending receipt
;;   119.01.xxx  IVA acreditable PAGADO        — input ITC, fully claimable
;;   119.02.xxx  IVA acreditable PENDIENTE     — input ITC, pending payment
;;
;; A separate "payment-side" flow (out of this commit's scope) moves
;; balances from 208.02 → 208.01 and from 119.02 → 119.01 when the
;; matching AR / AP is settled.
;;
;; IEPS (Impuesto Especial sobre Producción y Servicios) — federal
;; excise on tobacco, alcohol, fuels, sugary drinks, junk food. The
;; chart provides the holding accounts; rate selection is per-product
;; (out of scope here, see the tax-compute module).
;;
;; Retenciones — withholding at the point of payment (gobierno, large
;; taxpayers, services). Two pairs (IVA + ISR) on both sides.
;;
;; Tag conventions (`:mx-dpi-...`) let the DPI / DIOT aggregators pull
;; line totals without hard-coded code lookups.
;;
;; Schema fields per account:
;;   :code            — dot-separated SAT code (e.g. "208.01.001")
;;   :path            — hierarchical PTA-notation path
;;   :type            — :asset | :liability | :equity | :income | :expense
;;   :name            — Spanish label (per SAT Anexo 24)
;;   :reconcilable?   — true for AR/AP/Bancos/Caja
;;   :tax-recoverable?— true for IVA acreditable (ITC) accounts
;;   :tax-payable?    — true for IVA trasladado + IEPS payable accounts
;;   :tags            — vector of tag keywords for report aggregation
;;
;; Public sources (non-copyrightable):
;;   - Anexo 24 RMF (SAT)            — Código Agrupador del SAT
;;   - Ley del IVA, Art. 1-B          — cash-basis recognition
;;   - Ley del IEPS                   — excise scope
;;   - Ley del ISR, Art. 11 + Art. 76 — fiscal-year + retentions

